WEBVTT

00:00:02.581 --> 00:00:07.275
The plan sets the hill. Telo Ride now sends each level as the bike's target

00:00:07.275 --> 00:00:08.263
resistance.

00:00:10.324 --> 00:00:17.544
For an Echelon, level twelve is F0, B1, 01, 0C, AE, written with a response. Level

00:00:17.544 --> 00:00:19.781
thirty-two ends in C2.

00:00:20.647 --> 00:00:24.989
A target outside one to thirty-two is clamped before it's sent, and a fraction

00:00:24.989 --> 00:00:26.848
rounds to the nearest level.

00:00:30.971 --> 00:00:35.291
When the bike acknowledges the write, the time it took is kept with the command, in

00:00:35.291 --> 00:00:36.268
milliseconds.

00:00:41.295 --> 00:00:46.206
On the simulated bike, level fourteen goes out, and the very next resistance frame

00:00:46.206 --> 00:00:47.824
reports fourteen back.

00:00:51.618 --> 00:00:56.596
The target is the plan's level. The resistance is what the bike reports. Telo Ride

00:00:56.596 --> 00:00:57.928
keeps them apart.

00:01:01.942 --> 00:01:06.372
If the bike is away, the target is kept, and sent before anything else when it's

00:01:06.372 --> 00:01:06.949
back.

00:01:12.266 --> 00:01:17.959
An FTMS bike that refuses control stays read only. Its telemetry goes on, and the

00:01:17.959 --> 00:01:19.665
controls switch off.

00:01:22.590 --> 00:01:28.230
Still to come: raising and lowering by hand in slice 4.2, and the workout engine

00:01:28.230 --> 00:01:30.293
stepping the plan in 5.1.

00:01:32.913 --> 00:01:37.577
Home doesn't change yet, at any width. The targets go out from the engine, for the

00:01:37.577 --> 00:01:38.616
ride screens.

00:01:43.237 --> 00:01:47.952
What the tests prove: eleven new unit tests, one per row of the requirements, and

00:01:47.952 --> 00:01:49.591
every spec still green.

00:01:53.561 --> 00:01:58.164
Telo Ride, from the Telo family, turns a smart bike at home into a game.

00:01:58.509 --> 00:02:03.021
It pairs with the bike over Bluetooth, reads your power and sets resistance for

00:02:03.021 --> 00:02:04.692
every hill and interval.

00:02:05.037 --> 00:02:10.215
Two doors: Race (ride a map against your best-time ghost, bots or people) and

00:02:10.215 --> 00:02:15.663
Classes (ride along to a video, alone or with a group), fed by one progression of

00:02:15.663 --> 00:02:18.653
XP, rider levels, stars and map unlocks.

00:02:18.998 --> 00:02:21.491
A custom workout lives under Profile.
